EXPERIMENT 1.1 Contains Duplicate (217)
AIM :-Given an integer array nums, return true if any value appears at least twice in the array, and return false if every element is distinct.

ALGORITH :- 
1. Start.
2. Create an empty unordered set s.
3. Traverse the array nums from the first element to the last.
4. For each element:
    Check if the element is already present in the set.
    If it is present, return True because a duplicate is found.
    Otherwise, insert the element into the set.
5. If the loop finishes without finding any duplicate, return False.
6. End.

CODE :-
class Solution {
public:
    bool containsDuplicate(vector<int>& nums) {
        unordered_set<int> s;

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {
            if (s.find(nums[i]) != s.end()) {
                return true;
            }
            s.insert(nums[i]);
        }
        return false;
    }
};


EXPERIMENT 1.2 Contains Dupitcate-II (219)

AIM:- Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return true if there are two distinct indices i and j in the array such that nums[i] == nums[j] and abs(i - j) <= k.

ALGORTHM :-
1. Start
2. Create an empty unordered map mp.
3. Traverse the array from index 0 to n-1.
4. For each element:
    Check whether the element already exists in the map.
    If it exists:
      Calculate the difference between the current index and the stored index.
      If the difference is less than or equal to k, return True.
    Update the current index of that element in the map.
5. If the loop finishes without finding such a pair, return False.
6. End

CODE:-
class Solution {
public:
    bool containsNearbyDuplicate(vector<int>& nums, int k) {

        unordered_map<int, int> mp;

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

            if (mp.find(nums[i]) != mp.end()) {

                if (i - mp[nums[i]] <= k)
                    return true;
            }

            mp[nums[i]] = i;
        }

        return false;
    }
};
